UNIT tries_still_counted
KIND FUNCTIONAL
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
FIDELITY spec
ANCHOR this server's join page limit, set by the server's owner on 2026-11-17 ("100 per hour")
SIG tries_still_counted(times: list[i64], now: i64) -> list[i64]
ENVELOPE times is any list of moments, now is any moment; a moment is a whole number of milliseconds since 1970-01-01 UTC, and may be negative. times need not be in order and may repeat.
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION Which of one address's earlier join tries still count against it.
BEHAVIOR
R1 A try at moment t still counts when now - t is less than WINDOW. A try exactly WINDOW before now no longer counts.
R2 A try later than now (a clock that went back) still counts.
R3 The answer is the tries that still count, in the order they came in times, repeats kept. No try that counts gives an empty list.
PINNED const WINDOW = 3600000 CITED assumption the server's owner 2026-11-17: one hour, in milliseconds
PROVENANCE recorded by rdv from joinpage/tries_still_counted.go
